WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.304 --> 00:00:05.777
Why did I sell my first business?

00:00:05.777 --> 00:00:10.640
So I got a great question from one of my YouTube viewers (love you guys!), Burn Notice,

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:11.924
who wrote in to say:

00:00:11.924 --> 00:00:15.345
"Hey, Evan! I've got a question. I was just wondering why you sold your company."

00:00:15.345 --> 00:00:18.441
"You said in your last video that you were making good money and then you decided to sell it."

00:00:18.441 --> 00:00:22.516
"I was just wondering why. Couldn't you have evolved it and grew with your company? Thanks."

00:00:22.516 --> 00:00:25.932
So this is a great story and uh.. a great question!

00:00:25.932 --> 00:00:30.981
And the quick background, I had a biotech software company. I didn't start it, but I joined it, I became...

00:00:30.981 --> 00:00:37.518
an owner and the Chief Operating Officer; and I turned down big jobs, high paying jobs to do it.

00:00:37.518 --> 00:00:42.739
And my job was the marketing, the business development, basically making a business grow.

00:00:42.739 --> 00:00:48.053
And I turned it from making $300 a month, where I thought I was failing, thought of quitting,

00:00:48.053 --> 00:00:49.781
said I was going to quit.

00:00:49.781 --> 00:00:55.056
And turned it into a successful company with brand name clients, international presence and then sold it.

00:00:55.056 --> 00:00:59.238
That was all in... 3 years, so it was pretty fast.

00:00:59.238 --> 00:01:01.501
Why did I sell it? 2 main reasons, ok?

00:01:01.501 --> 00:01:07.981
The first was market opportunity. So if you look at most markets, you'll find that they expand and they...

00:01:07.981 --> 00:01:13.007
contract, they go like this. They go in waves of typically 8-15 year cycles.

00:01:13.007 --> 00:01:18.811
And you'll find that industries that have big companies, a few big companies,

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:23.442
they start the staggering. Those industries stag and then a lot of little inventors and entrepreneurs...

00:01:23.442 --> 00:01:25.903
come along and they make it exciting again.

00:01:25.903 --> 00:01:32.169
And then, slowly, it expands, lots of companies. And then people start acquiring, the big companies say:

00:01:32.169 --> 00:01:36.877
"Hey, we need to acquire these guys, we need to make this part of our business" and the market...

00:01:36.877 --> 00:01:40.678
starts to contract again and you get back to a few big players, and then it expands and then it c...

00:01:40.678 --> 00:01:44.139
So this happens a lot. You look at any industry over the years, this is what happens.

00:01:44.139 --> 00:01:49.045
And it was starting to happen in my industry, the big companies were coming in, scooping up...

00:01:49.045 --> 00:01:50.853
smaller companies.

00:01:50.853 --> 00:01:56.804
Some companies raised massive venture capital, there was a company that raised $800,000,000 to...

00:01:56.804 --> 00:02:00.042
go out and just start acquiring companies.

00:02:00.042 --> 00:02:07.695
So it was an exciting time and we had to make a decision to either sell now, where we could get a great...

00:02:07.695 --> 00:02:11.451
price for our company because there was so much interest,

00:02:11.451 --> 00:02:18.451
or have to wait another 8-15 years before this cycle happens again, and then be the only...

00:02:18.451 --> 00:02:20.133
independent player.

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:26.527
So, all of our competitors were getting scooped up and were being brought into massive corporations,

00:02:26.527 --> 00:02:29.444
and we would be the only little guy left.

00:02:29.444 --> 00:02:32.974
So that was one decision, one reason.

00:02:32.974 --> 00:02:37.902
The bigger reason, though... because the first one could be overcome, right?

00:02:37.902 --> 00:02:45.731
If we loved the business enough to last another 8-15 years or for as long as we lived, we could have...

00:02:45.731 --> 00:02:49.715
kept going, we could have overcome the obstacle of being the only small player.

00:02:49.715 --> 00:02:56.998
The main reason was my partners, so there were 3 of us in the business, my partners who started the...

00:02:56.998 --> 00:03:00.149
company, really wanted to get to the US.

00:03:00.149 --> 00:03:03.456
They wanted to live in the US, it was a personal decision.

00:03:03.456 --> 00:03:09.103
They live an alternate lifestyle, compared to most people.

00:03:09.103 --> 00:03:13.299
They believe in "un-schooling", not "homeschooling", "un-schooling".

00:03:13.299 --> 00:03:17.910
They were living a macrobiotic lifestyle and diet and...

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:24.010
did a whole bunch of different things... It was cool! Just an alternate way of living, compared to most people.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:30.853
And, you know, here in Toronto, there aren't too many people who live that kind of lifestyle,

00:03:30.853 --> 00:03:36.481
especially back then. So they wanted to get to California, because there were more people doing that...

00:03:36.481 --> 00:03:42.791
stuff, more people to connect with and learn from and share experiences with and, you know, for their kids...

00:03:42.791 --> 00:03:44.737
to grow up with.

00:03:44.737 --> 00:03:49.022
And so, it was a highly personal decision. And how do you tell somebody:

00:03:49.022 --> 00:03:54.698
"No, I don't want you to go live your dream! You can't do that!"? You know, "think about me!"

00:03:54.698 --> 00:04:01.840
You know, you can't do that. And so, the deal was finding a company that would acquire the business,

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:10.727
but then also bring on my 2 partners on a contract and sponsor them to stay in the United States,

00:04:10.727 --> 00:04:14.771
specifically in California. And so we made that happen. I stayed here.

00:04:14.771 --> 00:04:20.664
Nothing against the US, but I love Canada and I had lots of opportunities here to stick with.

00:04:20.664 --> 00:04:25.795
And I'm grateful, because it started me on my website and got me into venture capital and lead to the...

00:04:25.795 --> 00:04:29.778
#Believe movement and all that, so it was a good path to go down.

00:04:29.778 --> 00:04:33.570
But, uh... anyway, that's the story. I don't think I've ever told it before.

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:36.916
So that's why I sold, you know, that's why we sold the business.

00:04:36.916 --> 00:04:38.800
I thank you for letting me share that.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:40.326
Believe!

